title: 'frame-support: implement transaction chain batching via event field capture'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds opt-in chain batch capture to FRAME pallet events.

    ## New attributes

    Pallets can annotate their event enum with `#[pallet::capture_for_chain_batch]` and
    mark individual named variant fields with `#[chain_batch(capture = "name")]`. When
    `deposit_event` is called, the macro-generated implementation will SCALE-encode those
    fields and push them into the dispatch context alongside the normal event deposit. Any
    code running in the same dispatch can then retrieve and consume the captured data via
    `frame_support::dispatch_context::get_captured_event_fields()`.

    ```rust
    #[pallet::event]
    #[pallet::generate_deposit(pub fn deposit_event)]
    #[pallet::capture_for_chain_batch]
    pub enum Event<T: Config> {
        Transfer {
            #[chain_batch(capture = "amount")]
            amount: T::Balance,
            #[chain_batch(capture = "from")]
            from: T::AccountId,
            to: T::AccountId, // not captured
        },
    }
    ```

    ## New runtime API (`frame-support`)

    - `dispatch_context::capture_event_field(pallet, variant, field_name, encoded_bytes)` —
      called automatically by the generated `deposit_event`; no-op outside a dispatch context.
    - `dispatch_context::get_captured_event_fields() -> Option<Vec<CapturedEventEntry>>` —
      drains all captured entries for the current dispatch; returns `None` outside a context.
    - `dispatch_context::CapturedEventEntry` — public struct carrying `pallet`, `variant`,
      `field_name`, and the raw SCALE-encoded `value`.

crates:
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: minor
